<meta name="description" content="Capital Acquisition Brokers (CABs) are firms that engage in a limited range of activities, including but not limited to: advising companies and private equity funds on capital raising and corporate restructuring, andacting as a placement agent- or finder for sales of unregistered securities to institutional investors under limited conditions.providing fairness opinions, valuation services, and negotiation and structuring services. Firms that elect to be governed under the CAB rule set are not permitted, among other things, to participate or maintain an online platform in connection with Reg A or Reg Crowdfunding, carry or maintain customer accounts, handle customers’ funds or securities, accept" />
<link rel="canonical" href="https://www.finra.org/registration-exams-ce/capital-acquisition-brokers" />
